Source: packet
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Rifat Hasan Jihan <rjihan@users.noreply.github.com>
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/nozwock/packet
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 meson (>= 0.59),
 ninja-build,
 pkgconf,
 libglib2.0-dev (>= 2.66),
 libgtk-4-dev (>= 4.0.0),
 libadwaita-1-dev,
 desktop-file-utils,
 appstream,
# data/resources/meson.build compiles ui/*.blp with blueprint-compiler.
# dh_auto_configure runs meson with --wrap-mode=nodownload, so the
# subprojects/blueprint-compiler.wrap fallback is unavailable and the
# program has to come from the archive (trixie ships 0.16.0).
 blueprint-compiler (>= 0.16.0),
 gettext,
 protobuf-compiler,
# libdbus-sys (via rqs_lib -> bluer/btleplug) links the system libdbus and
# needs dbus-1.pc at build time.
 libdbus-1-dev,
 libssl-dev,
# The Rust toolchain (rustc + cargo) is intentionally NOT listed here.
# The CI workflow installs it via rustup so the compiler is not limited to
# whatever version Debian ships; dpkg-checkbuilddeps would fail on an apt
# "cargo" dependency that is satisfied out-of-band. If you build locally
# with Trixie's own toolchain, "apt install cargo" first.

Package: packet
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Quick Share client for Linux (GNOME)
 Packet lets you share files wirelessly with Android devices and other
 computers using the Quick Share protocol. It integrates with the GNOME
 desktop and is built with GTK4 and libadwaita.
 .
 This is an unofficial package built from a personal fork for
 Debian 13 (trixie).
